For Unix machines, here's one way to gently migrate players from one
version of nethack to the next.  Keep old versions and old save files
around, and use this script instead of the nethack shell script.  Once
a player finishes their saved game, they'll transparently start to
play the newest version.

This script was a quick hack, and it's lightly tested, but I'm pretty
sure it works reasonably well.  One thing that's missing: the -list
option should probably show all your saved games.

To use:

1. arrange so that each version's playground is put in
	some-directory/3.1.0
	some-directory/3.1.1
	etc.
(symlinks may help.)

2. Fix the value of $ROOT in the following Perl script.  Install this
script instead of nethack.sh.

3. add a notice to the "news" files in the old playgrounds, warning
users that they're playing an obsolete version.

4. delete the old playgrounds whenever you feel like it.

--cut here--
#!/usr/bin/perl

# vhack [-list]
# vhack [-version a.b.c] [nethack-options]

# This script will run either:
# a. the version specified with -version;
# b. the earliest version with a saved game for this uid;
# c. the latest version.

# The playground for each version is expected to be in
#	$ROOT/$version
# where $version is something like "3.1.0" or "3.1.1"

# Save files are found in	$ROOT/$version/$SAVE/
# The executable is 		$ROOT/$version/$HACK

$ROOT = "/usr/games/lib/nethacks";
$SAVE = "save";
$HACK = "nethack";
$MAXPLAYERS = 4;

# Some PAGER-fiddling nonsense.
if (!$ENV{'HACKPAGER'} && $ENV{'PAGER'}) {
	($pager, $options) = split(' ', $ENV{'PAGER'});
	$fullpager = &find_program($pager);
	if ($fullpager) {
		$ENV{'HACKPAGER'} = $fullpager;
	} else {
		print "Can't find $pager -- unsetting PAGER.";
		delete $ENV{'PAGER'};
		delete $ENV{'HACKPAGER'};
	}
}

if ($ARGV[0] eq '-version' || $ARGV[0] eq '-v') {
	shift @ARGV;
	&run(shift @ARGV, 'requested');
}

$uid = $<;
@versions = sort by_version eval 'chdir $ROOT && <*>';

if ($ARGV[0] eq '-list' || $ARGV[0] eq '-l') {
	print "available nethack versions:\n ", join("\n ", @versions), "\n";
	exit(0);
}

for $v (@versions) {
	next if ! -x "$ROOT/$v/$HACK";
	@saves = eval 'chdir "$ROOT/$v/$SAVE" && <*>';
	for $s (@saves) {
		($u) = $s =~ m/^(\d+)/;	# the uid from the file name.
		if ($u ne '' && $u == $uid) {
			&run($v, 'saved game');
		}
	}
}
&run(pop(@versions), "latest");

sub run {local ($v, $ident) = @_;
	print "$HACK version $v ($ident)...\n";

	local ($it) = "$ROOT/$v/$HACK";
	if ($MAXPLAYERS && $ARGV[0] ne '-s') {
		exec $it, @ARGV, $MAXPLAYERS;
	} else {
		exec $it, @ARGV;
	}
	die "$0: Couldn't run \"$it\": $!\n";
}

sub by_version {
	local (@a, @b);
	@a = split(/\./, $a);
	@b = split(/\./, $b);
	while (@a && $a[0] == $b[0]) {
		shift @a;
		shift @b;
	}
	$a[0] <=> $b[0];
}

sub find_program {local ($x) = @_;
	return $x if -x $x;
	for $p (split(':', $ENV{'PATH'})) {
		return "$p/$x" if -x "$p/$x";
	}
	return $x;
}


